id: pm-rl-s44k
title: Execute deterministic bandit policy updates across promoted generations
description: "Implement an opt-in TypeScript execution foundation for the recursive controller: a real two-action contextual bandit policy-gradient update, deterministic on-policy collection, separate evaluation examples, bounded generations and samples, checkpoint identities and successor reuse. This is a small numerical adapter, not an LLM trainer, durable controller, hosted training service or new CLI command."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: adapter,execution,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-09-07T22:57:50.791Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T23:06:04.837Z"
assignee: codex-pm-native
claim_principal: codex-pm-native
author: codex-pm-native
acceptance_criteria: Two generations change actual policy weights and the second collection receipt binds the first promoted checkpoint; identical inputs replay identical receipts; evaluation examples never contribute to gradient updates; invalid input and shared dataset identities refuse before work; a candidate that regresses or fails the declared gap bound stops recursion; new runtime source has exact four-metric coverage
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T23:06:04.837Z",codex-pm-native,"Implementation evidence 2026-09-07 UTC: eight real numerical tests pass, including an independently calculated one-sample REINFORCE gradient. The packed 57-file npm artifact executes through the public package export on Node 24.19.0 and Bun with byte-identical JSON receipts. Three accepted generations consume 768 samples and change weights from 0 to 0.1240234375, 0.24036581167552068 and 0.36331123588596426; evaluation expected rewards rise from 0.5 to 0.5247843586553662, 0.5479255767381022 and 0.5721550086836353. Generation two sources the exact first candidate digest. c8 independently reports bandit.ts 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Typecheck, ESLint, zero duplication, 19-file/134-declaration docstrings, production audit, approved identities and publish-attestation checks pass. Full package coverage and exact-head PR review remain pending; this does not establish LLM training or a durable execution controller."
